<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rimush</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rimush was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akkadian-empire">Akkadian Empire</a> and a son and successor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-of-akkad">Sargon of Akkad</a>. His reign was dominated by campaigns to suppress revolts among the Sumerian cities and other subject territories. Both Rimush and his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manishtushu">Manishtushu</a> were assassinated, illustrating the empire's dependence on the personal military ability of its rulers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rimush.jpg" alt="Rimush" width="320" height="239" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zunkir · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jar_fragment_Rimush_Tell_Brak_127340.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
